Third-party attributions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository vendors no third-party source. All external dependencies
are consumed as unmodified crates.io / PyPI packages resolved at build
time (see Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and claude-worker/pyproject.toml) and
carry their own licenses; they are not redistributed in this source tree.

Attribution for dependencies linked into a distributed *binary* is
generated at release time into THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md via `make
license-deps` (cargo-about). No compiled binary may be distributed
without LICENSE, NOTICE and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md alongside it.
See docs/arch/license-audit-2026-08-27.md §G5.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Runtime artifacts fetched by hash (Kronos forecast sidecar)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The optional forecast sidecar runs the Kronos time-series model. Its code
and weights are NOT vendored here and are NOT redistributed by this
project: claude-worker/kronos.lock pins them by sha256, and
`python -m claude_worker.kronos install` fetches them from their origin
into ~/multivenue/vendor/kronos/ and ~/multivenue/artifacts/kronos/,
outside this repository, refusing anything whose hash does not match.

  * Kronos (github.com/shiyu-coder/Kronos, commit 67b630e) — MIT.
    The upstream files are used unmodified; the installer also fetches
    and stores the project's own LICENSE beside them.
  * Kronos model weights (huggingface.co/NeoQuasar/Kronos-mini,
    -small, -base and the Kronos-Tokenizer-2k / -base quantizers) —
    released by the same project under the same MIT terms.

Neither is linked into any binary this project distributes: the engine
never loads them, and the sidecar is offline Python. THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
is therefore unaffected — it is generated by cargo-about from the Cargo
graph for the shipped targets and lists no Python package.

The `kronos` dependency group in claude-worker/pyproject.toml (torch,
numpy, pandas, einops, huggingface_hub, tqdm, safetensors) is likewise
optional and, like every other Python dependency, is consumed as
unmodified PyPI packages under their own licenses (BSD-3-Clause, MIT and
Apache-2.0) rather than redistributed here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Cryptographic primitives that would normally be pulled from a third-party
stack are handwritten in-tree and are original work of this project:

  * crates/core-crypto   — SHA-256, HMAC-SHA256, base64 (RFC 4648)
  * crates/signer-eip712 — EIP-712 typed-data signing over the secp256k1
                           and tiny-keccak crates (deliberately NOT
                           ethers or alloy)
